@model BillingMadeEasy.Web.Pages.Catalog.IndexModel
@using BillingMadeEasy.Web.Features.Catalog
@using BillingMadeEasy.Web.Infrastructure.Formatting
@{ var r = Model.Result; }
@if (r.Total == 0)
{
    <section class="empty">
        <span class="ms empty-icon" aria-hidden="true">@(Model.Q is null ? "inventory_2" : "search_off")</span>
        <h2>@(Model.Q is null ? "Nothing in the catalog yet" : $"Nothing matches “{Model.Q}”")</h2>
        <p class="muted">Add what you sell once, with its price, GST rate and HSN or SAC code. Every invoice line then fills itself in.</p>
        @if (Model.Can("Catalog.Offering.Manage"))
        {
            <a class="btn primary" href="/Catalog/Item?type=@(Model.Type ?? "product")@(Model.Q is null ? "" : "&name=" + Uri.EscapeDataString(Model.Q))">
                <span class="ms" aria-hidden="true">add</span>@(Model.Q is null ? "Add an item" : $"Add “{Model.Q}”")
            </a>
        }
    </section>
}
else
{
    <p class="result-count muted" aria-live="polite">@r.Total.ToString("N0") @(r.Total == 1 ? "item" : "items")</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="grid-table" data-row-nav>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Item</th>
                    <th scope="col">HSN / SAC</th>
                    <th scope="col">GST</th>
                    @if (Model.CanSeePrices) { <th scope="col" class="num">Price</th> }
                    <th scope="col">Unit</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var o in r.Rows)
                {
                    <tr data-href="/Catalog/Item/@o.OfferingId" tabindex="0" class="@(o.IsActive ? null : "inactive")">
                        <td>
                            <a href="/Catalog/Item/@o.OfferingId" class="row-link" tabindex="-1">@o.OfferingName</a>
                            @if (!o.IsActive) { <span class="badge">Hidden</span> }
                            @if (o.IsRecurring) { <span class="badge">Recurring</span> }
                            <span class="sub">@string.Join(" · ", new[] { OfferingType.Label(o.OfferingType), o.OfferingCode, o.BrandName, o.CategoryName }.Where(x => !string.IsNullOrEmpty(x)))</span>
                        </td>
                        <td class="mono">@(o.HsnSacCode ?? "—")</td>
                        <td>
                            @if (o.IsPureAgent) { <span class="badge">Outside GST</span> }
                            else if (o.TaxRateId is null) { <span class="badge warn">No GST rate</span> }
                            else { <span>@o.TaxName</span> }
                        </td>
                        @if (Model.CanSeePrices)
                        {
                            <td class="num">
                                @if (!o.HasPrice) { <span class="badge warn">No price</span> }
                                else { <span>@Money.Inr(o.DefaultPrice)</span><span class="sub">@(o.IsPureAgent ? "at cost" : o.TaxRateId is null ? "" : o.IsPriceInclusive ? "incl. GST" : "+ GST")</span> }
                                @if (o.PriceListCount > 0) { <span class="sub">@o.PriceListCount customer price@(o.PriceListCount == 1 ? "" : "s")</span> }
                            </td>
                        }
                        <td>@o.UnitCode</td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    @if (r.Pages > 1)
    {
        <nav class="pager" aria-label="Pages">
            @if (r.Page > 1) { <a href="@Model.Link(page: r.Page - 1)" rel="prev" data-key="[">‹ Previous <kbd>[</kbd></a> }
            <span class="muted">Page @r.Page of @r.Pages</span>
            @if (r.Page < r.Pages) { <a href="@Model.Link(page: r.Page + 1)" rel="next" data-key="]">Next › <kbd>]</kbd></a> }
        </nav>
    }
}
